abstract: >-
  A vulnerability scanner for Model Context Protocol codebases, released with a
  benign control corpus so that its false-positive rate is measurable rather than
  assumed. Detection covers four layers (LLM, Agentic AI, MCP, and traditional web),
  runs offline with no API key, and scores every finding with a computed CVSS v4.0
  vector and an SSVC priority rather than model-generated prose. The accompanying
  benchmark pairs a confirmed-exploitable ground truth with 285,463 lines of
  officially maintained MCP code containing none of the vulnerability classes under
  test, which is what makes precision computable at all.
